  "latest": {
    "version": "0.20.3",
    "notes": "Ancilla v0.20.3 \u2014 Deep research. Agents in view.\n\nAn open-source desktop and web workspace for Muse Code by AMAZONIA WORKS, available on Windows, macOS and Linux.\n\n**Deep Research:** investigate questions with parallel workers, follow their searches and sources, and save cited reports as PDF, Word or HTML. **Crew:** follow ordinary prompts and tools alongside workflows, native agents and background tasks, with timelines, live status and controls for work that needs you.\n\n**New in 0.20.3**\n- Linux **.deb and .rpm installers** add Ancilla to your application menu and install its system dependencies. Node.js remains private to the app.\n- **Install Muse Code inside Ancilla**, follow any browser approval, sign in with your Meta subscription, then choose a project folder. Setup includes progress, cancellation and retry.\n- **Fix for the Linux UnsafePath thread-start error:** Ancilla safely prepares the selected account's Muse data-folder permissions before starting work, preserving login, history and deletion records.\n- **Fresh subscription limits from Meta:** supported Muse browser logins refresh five-hour and weekly quota without a model call. Account selection stays fixed; missing or expired readings show as unknown.\n- Optional **desktop shortcuts**, plus one-click AppImage installation to a permanent location with an application-menu icon.\n- Muse is detected after installation even when the desktop PATH omits it. Package installations use package updates; AppImages retain signed automatic updates.\n\nRead [what changed in this release](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.3/docs/CHANGELOG.md) or [explore the interface](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.3/README.md).\n\n**What you need.** Ancilla bundles Node.js. On Linux, choose **Install Muse Code** in the app if needed. On Windows and macOS, setup provides Meta's installation command. Then choose **Sign in with Meta** and approve access using the account that owns your Muse Code plan. An existing Muse login is reused. Windows supports native Muse or Muse inside WSL2.\n\n**Which file.** Windows: `x64-setup.exe`. macOS, Apple Silicon and Intel: `universal.dmg`. Linux x86_64: **amd64.deb** for Ubuntu/Debian/Mint or **x86_64.rpm** for Fedora and compatible distributions; open it with your software installer, then launch Ancilla from the application menu. For a portable copy, use **amd64.AppImage**, allow executing it in your file manager, and open it; setup can install its launcher. If FUSE is unavailable, run it with `--appimage-extract-and-run`. Desktop shortcuts are available in **Settings \u2192 Linux setup**; some desktops require right-clicking the shortcut and choosing **Allow Launching**.\n\n**Updates.** Windows, macOS and AppImage builds accept only updates signed with Ancilla's key. For `.deb` and `.rpm`, download and open the next package; Settings links to the latest release.\n\n**Unsigned installers.** The Windows installer is not Authenticode-signed yet, so SmartScreen may warn about an unrecognised app: choose More info, then Run anyway. The macOS app is not notarized by Apple yet, so its first launch needs a right-click on the app, then Open.\n\n**Licenses.** Ancilla is free software under the [GNU AGPL v3](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.3/LICENSE). Portions derive from Helicon, Copyright (c) 2026 Harjot Singh Rana and contributors, under the MIT License; its notice is kept in [LICENSE-HELICON](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.3/LICENSE-HELICON). The third-party software each build bundles, Node.js among it, is listed with its licenses in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](https://github.com/aleff-ferreira/ancilla/blob/v0.20.3/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), which also ships inside the app.",
    "pub_date": "2026-09-29T07:31:01.757Z",
